{"text": "Brian Robertson\n\n(b) (6)\n\nExperienced developer of policy and communications strategy who excels at working within a team to achieve results\n\nCRISPIN SOLUTIONS, LLC Washington, D.C.\nPresident and CEO Oct. 2015\u2014present\ne Direct boutique firm serving unique client needs in the areas of communications, government relations, and\npolicy development.\n\nVENN STRATEGIES Washington, D.C.\nConsultant Jan. 2015\u2014Dec. 2015\ne Developed more effective communications strategies for major client, achieved marked increase in coverage\n\nED GILLESPIE FOR SENATE Virginia\nPolicy Director April 2014-Nov. 2014\ne Led the development of the candidate's widely praised and influential policy agenda\ne Collaborated with other top aides on a campaign strategy that came within 16,000 votes of unseating\nincumbent Senator Mark Warner, despite being outspent two to one\ne Organized briefings for the candidate for all campaign events, including joint forums and debates\ne Drafted major policy speeches, op-eds, and talking points\ne Recruited and collaborated with team of high-level Capitol Hill and think tank policy experts to consult with the\ncampaign\ne Worked with Digital Director to maintain an aggressive digital policy presence, including website, Facebook\npage, Twitter account, YouTube channel, blog and email outreach program\n\nUNITED STATES SENATE Washington, D.C.\nSenior Policy Advisor for Joint Economic Committee May 2009-April 2014\ne Developed successful communication strategy for the committee on a wide variety of economic issues,\nresulting in high-visibility placement of op-eds for members, promulgating the research of staff economists\ne Wrote speeches, research papers, talking points, and backgrounder briefs for members of the committee\n\nSenior Policy Advisor and Speechwriter for Senator Sam Brownback (R-KS) March 2004-May 2009\ne Drafted all major speeches on every policy topic, foreign and domestic\ne Managed all editorial projects, including books, magazine articles, and op-eds\ne Served as Senator's chief advisor on wide variety of domestic policy issues\ne Led the formulation of legislative policy and political and communications strategy, and on human trafficking,\nchild care, disabilities, tax reform, regulatory matters, and the economic impact of policy on family structure\n\nFAMILY POLICY REVIEW Washington, D.C.\nManaging Editor, Research Fellow Dec. 2002-March 2004\ne As Director of Publications, edited all publications, as well as managing the editorial team\ne Co-founded the quarterly Family Policy Review, conceived, solicited, and edited contributions\ne Published original research and policy agenda on work-family balance, tax policy, and family-friendly\nworkplace policy\n\nKOHLER FELLOW Rockford, IL\nDec. 2001-Dec. 2002\ne Awarded first annual fellowship at prestigious policy research center to write second book, published in 2003\n\nREGNERY PUBLISHING Washington, DC\nEditor Aug. 2000-Dec. 2001\ne Edited best-selling books for numerous prominent authors\n\nMAJOR PUBLISHED WORKS\ne Day Care Deception, Encounter Books, 2003\ne \u2014 There\u2019s No Place Like Work, Spence Publishing, 2000\n\nEDUCATION\nGeorge Mason University, Fairfax, VA. BA in History. Honors: Dean\u2019s List, Phi Alpha Theta. May 1987\nNational Journalism Center, \u201887",
